  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Call the line",
  "description": "A square with cones in the corners. Let the players give each side a name, for example four countries, animals or football clubs. Everyone has a ball and dribbles around inside the square.\n\nWhen the coach calls a name, everyone dribbles as fast as they can to that side and stops the ball on the line. After a while the coach can call a new name before the players arrive, so they have to turn with the ball. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up – listen and see where you are going."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Dribble with the outside of the foot or your laces when you want speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Turn with the sole or the inside when the name changes."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
